# Normalise every text file to LF *in the repository*, whatever the
# contributor's platform or core.autocrlf setting. Without this the repo's
# line endings depend on each clone's local Git config: a Windows contributor
# with autocrlf unset commits CRLF, and those carriage returns then travel
# into the Linux container images built from this tree.
#
# `text=auto` only governs what is stored. Checkout still follows the local
# config, so a Windows worktree keeps CRLF and nothing about the existing
# working copy churns.
* text=auto

# These are read inside Linux containers, where a stray CR is not whitespace
# but part of the token — a `RUN` continuation or an interpreter path. Pin
# them to LF in the working tree as well, so they are correct even when
# edited on Windows and mounted straight into a build.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.gpu  text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Generated lockfiles. Kept as text so diffs stay readable, but they should
# never be hand-edited, and marking them here keeps them out of language
# statistics and collapsed in review.
pixi.lock                  text linguist-generated=true
frontend/package-lock.json text linguist-generated=true
